/*
 * Event-B context of the Ecore package lending (http://example.org/lending), in CamilleX notation.
 *
 * Rodin compiles this file into the context lending_ctx once it is in an Event-B project with the CamilleX
 * plug-in installed.
 *
 * The carrier set OBJECT holds all objects that can exist, and enumerations are carrier sets partitioned by
 * their literals. The machine lending_machine sees this context and declares the population of every class and
 * every feature as variables, since objects come and go.
 *
 * Not exported:
 *  - operations: Member.canBorrow
 *  - derived and volatile features: Member.loanCount
 *  - the order and repetition of the values of many-valued features: features are relations
 *  - the structure of strings: they are elements of the carrier set STRING that only support equality
 *  - the structure of values of the data types EDouble: they are elements of carrier sets
 *
 * Integers are mathematical integers without bounds. Event-B carrier sets are not empty, so there is at least one
 * possible object, which need not belong to any class.
 */
context lending_ctx
sets
  OBJECT
  STRING
  Status
  EDouble
constants
  Status_AVAILABLE
  Status_ON_LOAN
  Status_WITHDRAWN
axioms
  @OBJECT_finite: finite(OBJECT)
  @Status_literals: partition(Status, {Status_AVAILABLE}, {Status_ON_LOAN}, {Status_WITHDRAWN})
end
